edit&amp;section=75\" title=\"Edit section: See also\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/2026_United_States_elections\" title=\"2026 United States elections\">2026 United States elections</a>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/2026_United_States_Senate_elections\" title=\"2026 United States Senate elections\">2026 United States Senate elections</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/2026_United_States_gubernatorial_elections\" title=\"2026 United States gubernatorial elections\">2026 United States gubernatorial elections</a></li></ul></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/119th_United_States_Congress\" title=\"119th United States Congress\">119th United States Congress</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/120th_United_States_Congress\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"120th United States Congress\">120th United States Congress</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/2025_Texas_redistricting\" title=\"2025 Texas redistricting\">2025 Texas redistricting</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/2025%E2%80%932026_United_States_redistricting\" title=\"2025–2026 United States redistricting\">2025–2026 United States redistricting</a></li></ul>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=76\" title=\"Edit section: Notes\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r1327269900\">.mw-parser-output .reflist-columns-2{column-width:30em}.mw-parser-output .reflist-columns-3{column-width:25em}body.skin-vector-2022 .mw-parser-output .reflist-columns-2{column-width:27em}body.skin-vector-2022 .mw-parser-output .reflist-columns-3{column-width:22.5em}.mw-parser-output .references[data-mw-group=upper-alpha]{list-style-type:upper-alpha}.mw-parser-output .references[data-mw-group=upper-roman]{list-style-type:upper-roman}.mw-parser-output .references[data-mw-group=lower-alpha]{list-style-type:lower-alpha}.mw-parser-output .references[data-mw-group=lower-greek]{list-style-type:lower-greek}.mw-parser-output .references[data-mw-group=lower-roman]{list-style-type:lower-roman}.mw-parser-output div.reflist-liststyle-upper-alpha .references{list-style-type:upper-alpha}.mw-parser-output div.reflist-liststyle-upper-roman .references{list-style-type:upper-roman}.mw-parser-output div.reflist-liststyle-lower-alpha .references{list-style-type:lower-alpha}.mw-parser-output div.reflist-liststyle-lower-greek .references{list-style-type:lower-greek}.mw-parser-output div.reflist-liststyle-lower-roman .references{list-style-type:lower-roman}</style><div class=\"reflist reflist-lower-alpha\"><div class=\"mw-references-wrap mw-references-columns\"><ol class=\"references\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-1\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">As well as five of the six <a href=\"/wiki/Delegate_(United_States_Congress)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Delegate (United States Congress)\">non-voting delegates</a>.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-Independents1-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">^ <a href=\"#cite_ref-Independents1_2-0\"><sup><i><b>a</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-Independents1_2-1\"><sup><i><b>b</b></i></sup></a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Kevin_Kiley_(politician)\" title=\"Kevin Kiley (politician)\">Kevin Kiley</a>, who was re-elected as a Republican in 2024, is an <a href=\"/wiki/Political_Independent\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Political Independent\">independent</a> who <a href=\"/wiki/Independent_Republican_(United_States)\" title=\"Independent Republican (United States)\">caucuses with the Republicans</a>, and is not included in the number of seats held by Republicans.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-3\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-3\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">As a result of redistricting.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-4\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-4\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">As a result of death, resignation, or expulsion.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-85\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-85\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">Calculated by taking the difference of 100% and all other candidates combined.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-Davis-93\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">^ <a href=\"#cite_ref-Davis_93-0\"><sup><i><b>a</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-Davis_93-1\"><sup><i><b>b</b></i></sup></a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">Davis was elected to a previous, competitive, version of this district which Trump only won by 3.2 points in 2024, but it was redrawn to be more strongly Republican-leaning in 2025 by the North Carolina state legislature.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-Kaptur-94\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">^ <a href=\"#cite_ref-Kaptur_94-0\"><sup><i><b>a</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-Kaptur_94-1\"><sup><i><b>b</b></i></sup></a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">Kaptur was first elected to a previous, competitive but Republican-tilting, version of this district which Trump won by 6.7 points in 2024, but it was redrawn to be more strongly Republican-leaning by a bipartisan redistricting commission, as the previous maps expired in 2024.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-Cuellar-95\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">^ <a href=\"#cite_ref-Cuellar_95-0\"><sup><i><b>a</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-Cuellar_95-1\"><sup><i><b>b</b></i></sup></a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">Cuellar was elected to a previous, competitive but Republican-tilting, version of this district which Trump only won by 7.3 points in 2024, but it was redrawn to be more strongly Republican-leaning in 2025 by the Texas state legislature.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-Gonzalez-96\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">^ <a href=\"#cite_ref-Gonzalez_96-0\"><sup><i><b>a</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-Gonzalez_96-1\"><sup><i><b>b</b></i></sup></a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">Gonzalez was elected to a previous, competitive but Republican-tilting, version of this district which Trump only won by 4.4 points in 2024, but it was redrawn to be more strongly Republican-leaning in 2025 by the Texas state legislature.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-kind-98\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">^ <a href=\"#cite_ref-kind_98-0\"><sup><i><b>a</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-kind_98-1\"><sup><i><b>b</b></i></sup></a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">Kiley was originally elected as a Republican. He left the Republican Party to become an independent in March 2026 but remains a member of the <a href=\"/wiki/House_Republican_Conference\" title=\"House Republican Conference\">House Republican Conference</a>.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-change-125\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-change_125-0\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">Competitive seats are defined as seats won by less than 10 points by their respective party in 2024</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-222\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-222\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">The 2026 edition of the Cook PVI includes redistricting changes in Missouri that were struck down by the Missouri Supreme Court in September 2026.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-221\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-221\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>210<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-229\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-229\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">Van Drew was first elected as a Democrat but switched to the Republican Party in December 2019.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-236\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-236\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">In Ohio, congressional candidates file with the board of elections of the most populous county in their districts, not with the Secretary of State.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-OH2026&#95;235-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-OH2026-235\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>222<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></span>\n</li>\n</ol></div></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"References\">References</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=77\" title=\"Edit section: References\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1327269900\" /><div>\n<div class=\"mw-references-wrap mw-references-columns\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-5\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-5\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r1333433106\">.mw-parser-output cite.citation{font-style:inherit;word-wrap:break-word}.mw-parser-output .citation q{quotes:\"\\\"\"\"\\\"\"\"'\"\"'\"}.mw-parser-output .citation:target{background-color:rgba(0,127,255,0.133)}.mw-parser-output .id-lock-free.id-lock-free a{background:url(\"//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/65/Lock-green.svg\")right 0.1em center/9px no-repeat}.mw-parser-output .id-lock-limited.id-lock-limited a,.mw-parser-output .id-lock-registration.id-lock-registration a{background:url(\"//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d6/Lock-gray-alt-2.svg\")right 0.1em center/9px no-repeat}.mw-parser-output .id-lock-subscription.id-lock-subscription a{background:url(\"//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/aa/Lock-red-alt-2.svg\")right 0.1em center/9px no-repeat}.mw-parser-output .cs1-ws-icon a{background:url(\"//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4c/Wikisource-logo.svg\")right 0.1em center/12px no-repeat}body:not(.skin-timeless):not(.skin-minerva) .mw-parser-output .id-lock-free a,body:not(.skin-timeless):not(.skin-minerva) .mw-parser-output .id-lock-limited a,body:not(.skin-timeless):not(.skin-minerva) .mw-parser-output .id-lock-registration a,body:not(.skin-timeless):not(.skin-minerva) .mw-parser-output .id-lock-subscription a,body:not(.skin-timeless):not(.skin-minerva) .mw-parser-output .cs1-ws-icon a{background-size:contain;padding:0 1em 0 0}.mw-parser-output .cs1-code{color:inherit;background:inherit;border:none;padding:inherit}.mw-parser-output .cs1-hidden-error{display:none;color:var(--color-error,#bf3c2c)}.mw-parser-output .cs1-visible-error{color:var(--color-error,#bf3c2c)}.mw-parser-output .cs1-maint{display:none;color:#085;margin-left:0.3em}.mw-parser-output .cs1-kern-left{padding-left:0.2em}.mw-parser-output .cs1-kern-right{padding-right:0.2em}.mw-parser-output .citation .mw-selflink{font-weight:inherit}@media screen{.mw-parser-output .cs1-format{font-size:95%}html.skin-theme-clientpref-night .mw-parser-output .cs1-maint{color:#18911f}}@media screen and (prefers-color-scheme:dark){html.skin-theme-clientpref-os .mw-parser-output .cs1-maint{color:#18911f}}</style><cite id=\"CITEREFSantalizNichols2026\" class=\"citation web cs1\">Santaliz, Kate; Nichols, Hans (March 2, 2026). <span class=\"id-lock-registration\" title=\"Free registration required\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.axios.com/2026/03/02/members-of-congress-retirements-record-high\">\"House retirements tied for most this century\"</a></span>. <i><a href=\"/wiki/Axios_(website)\" title=\"Axios (website)\">Axios</a></i>. <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20260303165503/https://www.axios.com/2026/03/02/members-of-congress-retirements-record-high\">Archived</a> from the original on March 3, 2026<span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">March 9,</span> 2026</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=Axios&amp;rft.atitle=House+retirements+tied+for+most+this+century&amp;rft.date=2026-03-02&amp;rft.aulast=Santaliz&amp;rft.aufirst=Kate&amp;rft.au=Nichols%2C+Hans&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.axios.com%2F2026%2F03%2F02%2Fmembers-of-congress-retirements-record-high&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2026+United+States+House+of+Representatives+elections\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-Pelosi-6\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">^ <a href=\"#cite_ref-Pelosi_6-0\"><sup><i><b>a</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-Pelosi_6-1\"><sup><i><b>b</b></i></sup></a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFRector2025\" class=\"citation web cs1\">Rector, Kevin (November 6, 2025). <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.latimes.com/politics/story/2025-11-06/rep-nancy-pelosi-former-house-speaker-wont-seek-another-term-in-2026\">\"Rep. Nancy Pelosi, trailblazing Democratic leader from San Francisco, won't seek reelection\"</a>. <i><a href=\"/wiki/Los_Angeles_Times\" title=\"Los Angeles Times\">Los Angeles Times</a></i><span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">November 6,</span> 2025</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=Los+Angeles+Times&amp;rft.atitle=Rep.+Nancy+Pelosi%2C+trailblazing+Democratic+leader+from+San+Francisco%2C+won%27t+seek+reelection&amp;rft.date=2025-11-06&amp;rft.aulast=Rector&amp;rft.aufirst=Kevin&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.latimes.com%2Fpolitics%2Fstory%2F2025-11-06%2Frep-nancy-pelosi-former-house-speaker-wont-seek-another-term-in-2026&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2026+United+States+House+of+Representatives+elections\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-Brownley-7\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">^ <a href=\"#cite_ref-Brownley_7-0\"><sup><i><b>a</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-Brownley_7-1\"><sup><i><b>b</b></i></sup></a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFHuey2026\" class=\"citation web cs1\">Huey, Makena (January 8, 2026). <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.vcstar.com/story/news/local/2026/01/08/u-s-rep-julia-brownley-will-not-seek-eighth-term-in-congress/88087843007/\">\"U.S. Rep. Julia Brownley announces she will not seek re-election\"</a>. <i><a href=\"/wiki/Ventura_County_Star\" title=\"Ventura County Star\">Ventura County Star</a></i><span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">January 8,</span> 2026</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=Ventura+County+Star&amp;rft.atitle=U.S.+Rep.+Julia+Brownley+announces+she+will+not+seek+re-election&amp;rft.date=2026-01-08&amp;rft.aulast=Huey&amp;rft.aufirst=Makena&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.vcstar.com%2Fstory%2Fnews%2Flocal%2F2026%2F01%2F08%2Fu-s-rep-julia-brownley-will-not-seek-eighth-term-in-congress%2F88087843007%2F&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2026+United+States+House+of+Representatives+elections\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-HolmesNorton-8\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">^ <a href=\"#cite_ref-HolmesNorton_8-0\"><sup><i><b>a</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-HolmesNorton_8-1\"><sup><i><b>b</b></i></sup></a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFWu2026\" class=\"citation web cs1\">Wu, Nicholas (January 25, 2026). <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.politico.com/news/2026/01/25/eleanor-holmes-norton-retires-dc-delegate-00731986?cid=apn\">\"Eleanor Holmes Norton won't seek reelection as DC delegate\"</a>. <i><a href=\"/wiki/Politico\" title=\"Politico\">Politico</a></i>.</cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=Politico&amp;rft.atitle=Eleanor+Holmes+Norton+won%27t+seek+reelection+as+DC+delegate&amp;rft.date=2026-01-25&amp;rft.aulast=Wu&amp;rft.aufirst=Nicholas&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.politico.com%2Fnews%2F2026%2F01%2F25%2Feleanor-holmes-norton-retires-dc-delegate-00731986%3Fcid%3Dapn&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2026+United+States+House+of+Representatives+elections\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-Wilson-9\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">^ <a href=\"#cite_ref-Wilson_9-0\"><sup><i><b>a</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-Wilson_9-1\"><sup><i><b>b</b></i></sup></a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFLillis2026\" class=\"citation web cs1\">Lillis, Mike (May 29, 2026). <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://thehill.com/homenews/house/5901250-frederica-wilson-retirement-florida/\">\"Florida Democrat Frederica Wilson to retire from the House\"</a>. <i>The Hill</i><span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">May 29,</span> 2026</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Hill&amp;rft.atitle=Florida+Democrat+Frederica+Wilson+to+retire+from+the+House&amp;rft.date=2026-05-29&amp;rft.aulast=Lillis&amp;rft.aufirst=Mike&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Fthehill.com%2Fhomenews%2Fhouse%2F5901250-frederica-wilson-retirement-florida%2F&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2026+United+States+House+of+Representatives+elections\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-Blair-10\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-Blair_10-0\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFKallis2026\" class=\"citation web cs1\">Kallis, Sarah (August 26, 2026). <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.gpb.org/news/2026/08/26/everton-blair-wins-13th-district-special-election-runoff\">\"Everton Blair wins 13th District special election runoff\"</a>. <i>GPB</i><span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">September 6,</span> 2026</span>. <q>November's general election will decide who represents the district for the next term, starting in January. Blair is not in that race...</q></cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=GPB&amp;rft.atitle=Everton+Blair+wins+13th+District+special+election+runoff&amp;rft.date=2026-08-26&amp;rft.aulast=Kallis&amp;rft.aufirst=Sarah&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.gpb.org%2Fnews%2F2026%2F08%2F26%2Feverton-blair-wins-13th-district-special-election-runoff&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2026+United+States+House+of+Representatives+elections\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-Robin-11\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">^ <a href=\"#cite_ref-Robin_11-0\"><sup><i><b>a</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-Robin_11-1\"><sup><i><b>b</b></i></sup></a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-styl